  "notes": {
    "nMobile": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "page": "mobile",
      "text": "What changes on a phone\n• Same model: top = information, bottom = action, slide first, webcams always visible\n• Updates collapse into one dashed “3 updates” chip; tapping it opens a sheet where each update jumps to the people or chat view that resolves it\n• Slide controls can’t rely on hover, so a small white pager sits under the slide (all slides · prev · 3/12 · next · annotate). Grid opens All slides, the pencil swaps the pager for a pen / highlighter / eraser toolbar with colours, Undo and Done, and the corner button minimizes the slide into a tile in the webcam grid (tap it to bring it back)\n• Webcams sit on top, capped at four so faces stay readable: the speaker, then raised hands by longest wait, then recent activity. “+10 · See all” opens everyone. Minimizing the slide is the explicit “show me the class” mode, so it shows all 14\n• Action bar: People & chat · Mic · Camera · React · More · Leave. React holds Raise hand, so the bar fits one thumb row\n• People and Chat become one bottom sheet with the same tabs, filters and status icons as desktop. Tap a student for a second sheet with every teacher action\n• Share media, notes, captions, breakout rooms, poll, timer, plugins, Learning Analytics and Room settings move into More",
      "w": 520,
      "x": 5190,
      "y": -300
    },
    "nMobileLand": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "page": "mobile",
      "text": "Landscape: the slide takes the left, webcams a two-column strip on the right, and controls sit under the slide. Sheets open from the right half so the slide stays visible.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 2772,
      "y": 1000
    },
    "note-aknqxs": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "page": "page-dpqe21",
      "text": "How the panel works\n• People and Chat open the same panel; segmented tabs at the top switch between them, and the bottom-bar button for the active tab lights up\n• Chat has an Everyone / Direct switch. Direct lists private conversations, with unread ones highlighted\n• Opening a conversation shows a private thread: a back arrow, a lock and ‘Direct message’ label, an ‘only you two can see this’ note, and a lock in the composer\n• Every person in People has a ‘Message privately’ button that jumps straight to their thread\n\nTry it in Play on any board: People tab → chat bubble on Frederick → back → Everyone.\n\nOpen question: should moderators be able to turn off private chat for a classroom? The thread note would then need to change.",
      "w": 480,
      "x": 547,
      "y": -356
    },
